Z||000000||TalShino||04-30-2000||11:31 PM||||would a V6 swap from a 87-88 Caviler be easy to do to a 88 2.5liter Fiero? what all would I need? Help!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||05-01-2000||03:17 PM||||The cavalier engine would physically fit, however there are a few problems to deal with. <BR>The cavalier uses a totally different engine management system that is more integrated into the wiring of the car than the fiero is, so you would have to dismantle the cavalier harness to remove the engine control parts from it. Then getting an exhaust system to work would be a problem because the cavalier uses the aluminum heads and the fiero v6 exhaust manifolds wont fit. Neither will the fiero's intake fit the aluminum head motor. <BR>It could be done, but it might be tough.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-01-2000||04:20 PM||||Actually cooter, I think cavaliers of that year used the same cast V6 Fiero does. At least the last mid 80's one I saw did. My first reaction on lifting the cars hood was Hey, that's a fiero motor. I don't think they put the aluminum jobs in untill 89-90 or there about when they changed the whole body style of the car as well. That or maybe there was a choice of V6 for them. The one we had was a Z24. 85 I think. F'ing thing never ran right the whole time she had it. The digital dash really sucked, when it whould even light up.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||05-01-2000||08:28 PM||||My mom bought an 87 Z-24 new. It has the DIS 2.8, mass air FI and AL heads. I was interested in using it in my Fiero until I saw the nightmare of wiring to be done.||||reg||1
